PAYLOAD={"batch_id":"sleepy-hollow-research-001","job_id":"SH-001-04","correlation_id":"sleepy-hollow-research-001:SH-001-04","term":"Master Hendrick Hudson","status":"VERIFIED_SEARCH_PATTERN_CANDIDATE","finding":"Irving's Master Hendrick Hudson refers to English explorer Henry Hudson. 'Hendrick' reflects the Dutch-context name. In 1609 Hudson sailed for Dutch interests/Dutch East India Company while seeking a passage to Asia and explored the river later bearing his name. In the tale, the allusion anchors the narrator's Dutch/New Netherland historical frame while retaining Irving's comic antiquarian voice.","evidence":[{"door":"primary/local-text","source":"Library of Congress digitized A Book of the Hudson / Irving text","claim":"Irving uses Master Hendrick Hudson in the Sleepy Hollow passage."},{"door":"official-institutional-history","source":"U.S. National Park Service Governors Island / Bard Rock histories","claim":"Henry Hudson sailed into New York waters in 1609 working for Dutch interests; NPS states he explored the Hudson under the Dutch East India Company while seeking the Northwest Passage."},{"door":"primary-voyage-record","source":"Library of Congress, Extract from the journal of the voyage of the Half-Moon, Henry Hudson, master, 1609","claim":"Institutional primary-source collection independently anchors Hudson and the Half-Moon voyage."},{"door":"annotated/context-source","source":"Owl Eyes historical-context annotation","claim":"Explains Hendrick as the Dutch-context form for Henry Hudson and connects the naming to the tale's Dutch narrator/frame."}],"search_pattern":{"name":"HISTORICAL-NAME IDENTITY BRIDGE","function":"When a historical person appears under a period, translated, localized, title-bearing, or variant name, do not search only the surface string. Bridge variant-name -> canonical identity -> institutional/primary history -> local narrative context -> function of the variant form.","steps":["capture exact surface name and title","search canonical/variant identity","verify identity with institutional or primary evidence","verify event/date relevant to local passage","compare why the text uses this form rather than modern canonical name","separate identity fact from interpretation of narrative function"],"reusable":true},"contradictions":"No material contradiction found on identity. Preserve distinction between Hudson being English by birth and sailing in Dutch service; do not collapse nationality and employer/patronage.","reader_aid_fit":"A brief note could identify Hendrick Hudson as Henry Hudson and mention the 1609 Dutch-sponsored voyage; deeper history is optional.","next_state":"WAREHOUSE_CANDIDATE_AFTER_FIT_TEST"}
